---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Contribute"
  description="How to contribute to nstate — scorecards, data pipelines, country chapters, and open-source tools for government accountability."
>
  <div class="container">
    <div class="page-header">
      <div class="breadcrumb">
        <a href="/">nstate</a> / <span>contribute</span>
      </div>
      <h1>Contribute</h1>
      <p class="page-sub">
        nstate is built by people who believe the evidence should be public and the
        methods should be checkable. You don't need to be an economist.
        If you can find a primary source and write a sentence, you can contribute.
      </p>
    </div>

    <hr class="divider" />

    <!-- Contribution types -->
    <section class="section">
      <div class="section-label">ways to contribute</div>
      <div class="contrib-grid">
        <div class="contrib-type">
          <div class="contrib-type__icon">01</div>
          <h3>Scorecard</h3>
          <p>Find a government programme with a measurable objective and public data. Write a scorecard following the methodology template. Submit a PR.</p>
          <div class="contrib-type__effort">
            <span class="effort-label">effort</span>
            <span class="badge badge--amber">high</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="contrib-type">
          <div class="contrib-type__icon">02</div>
          <h3>Data pipeline</h3>
          <p>Python or R script that fetches, cleans, and versions a government dataset to CSV/Parquet. Even a one-source pipeline is useful.</p>
          <div class="contrib-type__effort">
            <span class="effort-label">effort</span>
            <span class="badge badge--medium">medium</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="contrib-type">
          <div class="contrib-type__icon">03</div>
          <h3>Source verification</h3>
          <p>Check a published scorecard's data sources. Confirm the figure matches the original release. Report discrepancies via GitHub issue.</p>
          <div class="contrib-type__effort">
            <span class="effort-label">effort</span>
            <span class="badge badge--grey">low</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="contrib-type">
          <div class="contrib-type__icon">04</div>
          <h3>Country chapter</h3>
          <p>Adapt the methodology for your country's government data. Become a chapter maintainer.</p>
          <div class="contrib-type__effort">
            <span class="effort-label">effort</span>
            <span class="badge badge--amber">high</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="contrib-type">
          <div class="contrib-type__icon">05</div>
          <h3>Methodology challenge</h3>
          <p>Disagree with a counterfactual approach or evidence quality rating? Open a PR with a counter-analysis meeting the same evidence standards.</p>
          <div class="contrib-type__effort">
            <span class="effort-label">effort</span>
            <span class="badge badge--amber">high</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="contrib-type">
          <div class="contrib-type__icon">06</div>
          <h3>Shadow agent (Phase 3)</h3>
          <p>Build a shadow automation of a government administrative process. Must run in read-only mode initially. Agents recommend; they do not act.</p>
          <div class="contrib-type__effort">
            <span class="effort-label">effort</span>
            <span class="badge badge--amber">high</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <hr class="divider" />

    <!-- Scorecard PR process -->
    <section class="section">
      <div class="section-label">scorecard contribution</div>
      <h2>how to submit a scorecard</h2>
      <p class="section-sub">
        This is the core contribution type. Follow these steps exactly.
        A PR that skips a step will not be merged.
      </p>

      <div class="process">
        <div class="process-step">
          <div class="process-step__num">1</div>
          <div class="process-step__body">
            <h3>State your claim</h3>
            <p>
              Open a GitHub issue: "Scorecard: [policy name] [country]". State the policy,
              its stated objective (verbatim from official source), and the primary data
              source you will use. Wait for a maintainer to assign it to you — this
              prevents duplicate work.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="process-step">
          <div class="process-step__num">2</div>
          <div class="process-step__body">
            <h3>Find the data</h3>
            <p>
              Every figure must come from a primary official source. If a figure only
              appears in a news article, it does not qualify. If you cannot find primary
              data, close the issue and explain why — that is a valid outcome.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="process-step">
          <div class="process-step__num">3</div>
          <div class="process-step__body">
            <h3>Write the pipeline</h3>
            <p>
              Write a script in <code>country/pipelines/</code> that fetches the data
              from the primary source and outputs to <code>country/data/</code>.
              The pipeline must be reproducible from scratch with a single command.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="process-step">
          <div class="process-step__num">4</div>
          <div class="process-step__body">
            <h3>Complete the template</h3>
            <p>
              Copy <code>uk/scorecards/TEMPLATE.md</code>. Fill in all seven sections.
              Every section is mandatory. If you cannot complete a section with
              evidence-quality HIGH or MEDIUM, the evidence quality for that dimension
              is LOW or NOT MEASURABLE — write that.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="process-step">
          <div class="process-step__num">5</div>
          <div class="process-step__body">
            <h3>Open a PR</h3>
            <p>
              PR title: <code>[SCORECARD] [Country]: [Policy name]</code>.
              Include: the scorecard file, the data pipeline, and the raw data output.
              A maintainer will review source citations and evidence quality ratings.
              Expect back-and-forth — that is normal and expected.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <hr class="divider" />

    <!-- Country chapter process -->
    <section class="section" id="country-chapter">
      <div class="section-label">country chapters</div>
      <h2>start a national chapter</h2>
      <div class="chapter-steps">
        <div class="chapter-step">
          <strong>01 — open an issue</strong>
          <p>Title: "Country chapter: [country name]". Provide your name (or handle), country, primary data source for your first scorecard, and confirmation you have read the methodology.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="chapter-step">
          <strong>02 — fill the country template</strong>
          <p>Copy <code>COUNTRY-TEMPLATE.md</code> → <code>your-country/README.md</code>. List your country's primary statistical releases, the equivalent of OGL, and your first-wave scorecard priorities.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="chapter-step">
          <strong>03 — first scorecard</strong>
          <p>Submit at least one scorecard via PR following the full methodology. The chapter is not listed on the countries page until the first scorecard is merged.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="chapter-step">
          <strong>04 — governance</strong>
          <p>Chapter maintainers must disclose political affiliation or material conflicts relevant to the policies they audit. Independence is not optional — it is the methodology.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <hr class="divider" />

    <!-- Standards reminder -->
    <section class="section">
      <div class="section-label">standards</div>
      <h2>what we will not merge</h2>
      <ul class="no-list">
        <li>Figures without a primary source URL and data release date</li>
        <li>Scorecard verdicts that pre-determine the outcome before seeing the data</li>
        <li>Content that targets named individuals rather than programmes and policies</li>
        <li>Counterfactuals at Level 5 (descriptive only) presented as causal evidence</li>
        <li>Evidence quality ratings that overstate certainty</li>
        <li>Analysis of policies below £100m/year without demonstrated high public interest</li>
        <li>Scorecards where the contributing maintainer has an undisclosed material conflict</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <div class="cta-block">
      <div>
        <strong>Ready to start?</strong>
        <p>The repo is at github.com/nstate-project/nstate. Issues are the first step.</p>
      </div>
      <a href="https://github.com/nstate-project/nstate" class="btn btn--primary" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        go to github ↗
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .page-header {
    padding: 3rem 0 2rem;
  }

  .breadcrumb {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--text-3);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .breadcrumb a {
    color: var(--amber);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .page-header h1 {
    font-size: 2.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .page-sub {
    color: var(--text-2);
    max-width: 60ch;
  }

  .section {
    padding: 3rem 0;
  }

  .section-label {
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--amber);
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .section h2 {
    font-size: 1.6rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .section-sub {
    color: var(--text-2);
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    max-width: 60ch;
  }

  /* Contrib grid */
  .contrib-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(240px, 1fr));
    gap: 1px;
    background: var(--border);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .contrib-type {
    background: var(--bg);
    padding: 1.5rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.6rem;
  }

  .contrib-type__icon {
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--amber);
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }

  .contrib-type h3 {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .contrib-type p {
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--text-2);
    flex: 1;
    max-width: none;
  }

  .contrib-type__effort {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-top: auto;
    padding-top: 0.75rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .effort-label {
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    color: var(--text-3);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }

  .badge--medium {
    background: var(--amber-dim);
    color: var(--amber);
    opacity: 0.6;
  }

  /* Process */
  .process {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1px;
    background: var(--border);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .process-step {
    background: var(--bg);
    padding: 1.5rem;
    display: flex;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  .process-step__num {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--amber);
    min-width: 2rem;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    line-height: 1;
    padding-top: 0.15rem;
  }

  .process-step__body h3 {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }

  .process-step__body p {
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--text-2);
    max-width: none;
  }

  /* Chapter steps */
  .chapter-steps {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(240px, 1fr));
    gap: 2rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .chapter-step {
    border-top: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 1.25rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .chapter-step strong {
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--amber);
  }

  .chapter-step p {
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--text-2);
    max-width: none;
  }

  /* No list */
  .no-list {
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding: 1.5rem;
  }

  .no-list li {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--text-2);
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    position: relative;
    max-width: none;
  }

  .no-list li::before {
    content: '✕';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--text-3);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
  }

  /* CTA block */
  .cta-block {
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding: 2rem;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 4rem;
  }

  .cta-block strong {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
  }

  .cta-block p {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--text-2);
    max-width: none;
  }

  .btn {
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: var(--font);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    padding: 0.7rem 1.4rem;
    text-decoration: none;
    border: 1px solid transparent;
    transition: background 0.15s, color 0.15s;
  }

  .btn--primary {
    background: var(--amber);
    color: var(--bg);
    border-color: var(--amber);
  }

  .btn--primary:hover {
    background: #e6b800;
    color: var(--bg);
  }
</style>
